<title>FRANCE: Algeria raises milk price by 11 percent.</title>
<headline>Algeria raises milk price by 11 percent.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algeria raised the price of milk by 11 percent to 20 dinars (37 cents) a litre, effective Thursday morning, the Algerian state-run radio said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The authorities scrapped state subsidies on imported milk, sparking the increase from the current 18 dinars, said the radio quoting the trade ministry.</p>
<p>Algeria imports about 270,000 tonnes of milk products each year.</p>
<p>($1 = 54 dinars)</p>
</text>
